cowpager(1) "@VERSION@" "cowpager - cow pager"

# NAME

cowpager - FvwmPager-style visual pager for the cow window manager

# SYNOPSIS

*cowpager* [*-a* _anchor_] [*-h*]

# DESCRIPTION

*cowpager* connects to the cow window manager's status socket and
presents a floating layer-shell window showing all desks and pages
with miniature representations of window positions.

The pager updates in real time as desks, pages, and windows change.
Clicking a desk cell switches to that desk; clicking a page sub-cell
within the active desk switches to that page.

*cowpager* requires cow to be running and accessible via
_$XDG\_RUNTIME\_DIR/cow-status.sock_ and
_$XDG\_RUNTIME\_DIR/cow-cmd.sock_.

# OPTIONS

*-a* _anchor_
	Anchor position on the screen. Valid values:

	*top-right* (default), *top-left*, *bottom-right*, *bottom-left*

*-h*
	Print usage and exit.

# DISPLAY

Each desk is shown as a rounded rectangle labelled with its desk
number.  The currently active desk is highlighted in blue.

When the page grid is larger than 1×1 (configured via
*set desktop\_size N M*), each desk cell is subdivided into a grid of
page sub-cells.  The currently visible page is highlighted in green.

Miniature window positions are drawn within each page sub-cell at
proportional coordinates.  The focused window is shown in orange;
other windows in grey.  Windows on non-active desks show a count
rather than individual miniatures.

# INTERACTIVITY

- *Click a desk cell*: sends *desk -d N* to switch to that desk.
- *Click a page sub-cell*: sends *page -c col row* to switch to that
  page (only meaningful when the page grid is larger than 1×1).

# ENVIRONMENT

*XDG\_RUNTIME\_DIR*
	Used to locate the cow status and command sockets.

# EXAMPLE

Start cowpager in the top-right corner (the default):

```
cowpager &
```

Place it in the bottom-left:

```
cowpager -a bottom-left &
```

Launch from *cow.conf* so it starts with the session:

```
exec cowpager
```

# SEE ALSO

*cow*(1), *cowbar*(1), *moocow*(1)

